(07 ? AMAN PDF QUICK-REVISION CHEATSHEET \(STAFF/SENIOR APPLIED SCIENTIST / ML ENGINEER\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Built from: **Aman's AI Journal Interview Questions PDF**.) Tj
T*
(Goal: high-density review in **10?15 minutes** before interviews.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(0\) 2-minute review strategy) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Read sections **1, 2, 5** first \(highest interview hit rate\).) Tj
T*
(2. Then skim **3 and 4** for depth probes.) Tj
T*
(3. Use section **8** for formula recall and section **9** for rapid-fire.) Tj
T*
(4. If you get stuck in interview: answer with **definition -> intuition -> equation -> trade-) Tj
T*
(off -> failure mode**.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1\) Core ML + DL fundamentals \(must-answer cleanly\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Bias-variance tradeoff) Tj
T*
(? **Bias**: underfit, high training/test error.) Tj
T*
(? **Variance**: overfit, low train error, high test error.) Tj
T*
(? Control with model capacity, regularization, data size, augmentation.) Tj
T*
(? Staff-level answer includes **which knob** you would turn first and why.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(L1 vs L2 regularization) Tj
T*
(? L1 penalty: \\\(\\lambda \\sum_i |w_i|\\\) -> sparse weights, feature selection.) Tj
T*
(? L2 penalty: \\\(\\lambda \\sum_i w_i^2\\\) -> smooth shrinkage, stability.) Tj
T*
(? Use L2 as default for dense signals; L1 when sparsity/selection matters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why random initialization?) Tj
T*
(? Same initialization for all neurons in a layer -> identical gradients -> neurons remain) Tj
T*
(symmetric -> no diversity learned.) Tj
T*
(? Random init breaks symmetry and allows specialized feature learning.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why MSE is poor for classification) Tj
T*
(? MSE with sigmoid can yield slow gradients in saturated regions.) Tj
T*
(? Cross-entropy gives stronger, better-shaped gradients for probabilistic classification.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Batch / stochastic / mini-batch GD) Tj
T*
(? Batch GD: stable but slow per update.) Tj
T*
(? SGD: noisy but can escape sharp minima/saddles.) Tj
T*
(? Mini-batch: practical default; best throughput and convergence balance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2\) Transformers / LLMs / GenAI \(very common senior probes\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Self-attention in one line) Tj
T*
(? Computes context-aware token representations by weighted aggregation of all token values.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why Q, K, V?) Tj
T*
(? \\\(QK^\\top\\\) computes relevance scores \(who should attend to whom\).) Tj
T*
(? \\\(V\\\) holds payload to aggregate.) Tj
T*
(? Separating \\\(K\\\) and \\\(V\\\) decouples **matching** from **content**.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

