(Attention formula) Tj
T*
(? \\\(\\text{Attention}\(Q,K,V\)=\\text{softmax}\\left\(\\frac{QK^\\top}{\\sqrt{d_k}}\\right\)V\\\)) Tj
T*
(? \\\(\\sqrt{d_k}\\\) scaling prevents large dot products from saturating softmax.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Transformer drawbacks) Tj
T*
(? \\\(O\(n^2\)\\\) attention cost \(memory/latency bottleneck on long context\).) Tj
T*
(? Data-hungry; can hallucinate; inference expensive.) Tj
T*
(? Mitigations: sparse/linear attention, retrieval, chunking, KV-cache optimizations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Temperature / top-k / top-p) Tj
T*
(? Temperature controls sharpness of token distribution.) Tj
T*
(? top-k truncates to k most likely tokens.) Tj
T*
(? top-p \(nucleus\) truncates to smallest set with cumulative prob >= p.) Tj
T*
(? Higher values => more diversity, less determinism.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why same prompt can produce different outputs) Tj
T*
(? Sampling randomness + temperature/top-k/top-p + seed differences + backend nondeterminism.) Tj
T*
(? At near-zero temperature and fixed seed, outputs are more reproducible.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(DDPM vs DDIM) Tj
T*
(? DDPM: stochastic reverse process; more diverse, slower sampling.) Tj
T*
(? DDIM: deterministic/implicit trajectory; faster sampling, often less diversity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GAN mode collapse) Tj
T*
(? Generator maps many latent points to limited outputs \(low diversity\).) Tj
T*
(? Mitigate with improved objectives \(WGAN-GP\), minibatch discrimination, better D/G balance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(RLHF at high level) Tj
T*
(? SFT -> preference data -> reward model -> PPO/DPO-style optimization.) Tj
T*
(? Key risk: reward hacking / alignment tax / preference noise.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3\) Training pathologies + debugging checklist) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Overfitting mitigation stack \(in order\)) Tj
T*
(1. Data quality + leakage check.) Tj
T*
(2. Train/val split sanity \(no overlap, proper time split if needed\).) Tj
T*
(3. Regularization \(weight decay, dropout, label smoothing\).) Tj
T*
(4. Early stopping + learning-rate schedule.) Tj
T*
(5. Augmentation / more data.) Tj
T*
(6. Reduce model capacity or freeze lower layers in fine-tuning.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Vanishing gradients) Tj
T*
(? Deep nets with saturating activations or poor initialization can lose gradient signal.) Tj
T*
(? Fixes: ReLU-family activations, residual connections, normalization, careful initialization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Batch norm: why it helps) Tj
T*
(? Stabilizes optimization landscape and gradient flow.) Tj
T*
(? Enables larger learning rates and faster convergence.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Validation loss up while accuracy up) Tj
T*
(? Possible when confidence calibration worsens: more correct labels but overconfident wrong) Tj
T*
(predictions inflate log loss.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If test performance underperforms) Tj
T*
ET

